BASH TERMINAL COMMANDS
cd - change directory(folder); Syntax: cd(foldername)
ls(list all the content of a folder available)
pwd - print working directory -used to print the path of a directory

cd .. to go back a folder level. The two dots will take you back one level. 
more <filename> You can see what's in a file 

Clear - to empty the terminal
list contents of a folder/directory in long list format: ls =l <filename>

