>>Content

1. Restart Terminal
    echo <text> - used to print something in the terminal

2. Print Working Directory/folder
    ##(to see the path of the folder) - The output tells you where the folder you are in is located.
    pwd - eg /home/codeally/project

3. List - 
    ##used to find out what is in a folder/directory - The output is showing everything in this folder.
    ls
    
4. Change Directory
    ##used to go into a folder/directory - cd stands for "change directory
  ->   cd <folder_name> to go forward
  ->   cd .. used to go back a folder level 
  ->   cd ../.. used to go back 2 folders/directories. Each set of dots represents another folder level
    *** The . takes you to the folder you are in, and .. takes you back, or up, a folder. ***

12. More 
    ##used to see what's in a "file"
    more <filename>

13. Clear
    ##empty the terminal if it looks too cluttered

16. List + Flags [command <flag>]
    ##you can add a "flag" to a command to use it a differemt way
    -> ls -l list the contents of a folder in "long list format"
    -> -all list all the files in a folder/directory including hidden files and files without an extension
    -> --help Display the help menu for the command
**NOTE** In the Terminal, Folders appear in Blue, Files are normal white text, images appear in Pink

34. Make Directory
    mkdir <folder_name> used to make a new folder

